//! Detection engine for Korean personally identifiable information (PII).
//!
//! `krpii-core` locates PII such as phone numbers, resident registration
//! numbers, and card numbers, and rewrites them so that text can be safely
//! forwarded to LLMs or written to logs. Candidates are generated by permissive
//! patterns and then validated with checksums and date checks, which keeps the
//! false-positive rate low on numeric text such as order or tracking numbers.
//!
//! All offsets are UTF-8 **byte** offsets into the original `&str`. Language
//! bindings are responsible for converting them to their native string indices.
//!
//! # Examples
//!
//! ```
//! use krpii_core::{mask, MaskStyle};
//!
//! let text = "홍길동 010-1234-5678, 주민번호 900101-1234567로 가입";
//! assert_eq!(
//!     mask(text, MaskStyle::Partial),
//!     "홍길동 010-****-5678, 주민번호 900101-*******로 가입",
//! );
//! assert_eq!(mask(text, MaskStyle::Tag), "홍길동 <PHONE>, 주민번호 <RRN>로 가입");
//! ```
//!
//! Use [`Detector`] to restrict entity types or apply a confidence threshold:
//!
//! ```
//! use krpii_core::{Detector, EntityType};
//!
//! let detector = Detector::new().with_types([EntityType::Rrn]);
//! let entities = detector.detect("010-1234-5678 / 900101-1234567");
//! assert_eq!(entities.len(), 1);
//! assert_eq!(entities[0].entity_type, EntityType::Rrn);
//! ```

